PROPRIETARY — NOT OPEN SOURCE

This repository is a private library of the author's own work, harvested from
projects the author built. It is not published under an open-source licence, and
nothing here grants any permission to third parties.

No permission is granted to any person or organisation to copy, use, modify,
merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, or sell any part of this repository, or
any derivative of it, without the author's prior written permission.

WHY THIS IS DELIBERATE

Some of this code is commercial product. The ethnic-luxe stack in particular
ships Ed25519-signed licence keys, plan gating and per-tenant provisioning
specifically so the same codebase can be sold many times without losing control
of it. An open-source licence here would grant everyone the permission that
machinery exists to withhold — including the right to resell it.

If a specific module is ever worth releasing publicly (a standalone GSTIN
validator, say), release that file on its own terms. Do not relicense the
repository to do it.

CLIENT WORK

Shipping code from this repository into a project delivered to a client does not
require relicensing this repository, but it is a decision worth making
deliberately each time: grant the client a licence to USE the delivered work,
rather than transferring ownership of the underlying modules. Otherwise the same
module cannot be reused for the next client.

THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES

This repository contains no vendored third-party code. Packages referenced in
the manifest (express, ejs, sharp, react, @supabase/supabase-js, and others)
remain under their own licences and are not covered by this notice.

NO WARRANTY

The code is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. It was written for
specific projects and carries their assumptions; read the notes in each asset's
README before relying on it.
